## Description

For the aria2 download client integration, torrents that have finished downloading and are now only seeding are still reported with the `leeching` state instead of `seeding`, even though `seeding` is a valid state in `DownloadClientItem` (`packages/integrations/src/interfaces/downloads/download-client-items.ts`).

## Root cause

In `packages/integrations/src/download-client/aria2/aria2-integration.ts`, `getTorrentState` maps aria2's `active` status unconditionally to `leeching`:

```ts
private getTorrentState(aria2Status: Aria2Download["status"], isTorrent: boolean): DownloadClientItem["state"] {
    switch (aria2Status) {
      case "active":
        return "leeching";
      case "waiting":
        return "queued";
      case "paused":
        return "paused";
      case "complete":
        return "completed";
      case "error":
        return "failed";
      case "removed":
      default:
        return "unknown";
    }
}
```

aria2 itself doesn't distinguish "downloading" from "seeding" in its `status` field — both report as `active` while the torrent is active in the client (downloading, or seeding after completion but before seed-ratio/seed-time targets are reached). The completion state can be derived from the download's own progress instead: when `completedLength >= totalLength` (already available on the `Aria2Download` object used elsewhere in this file), an `active` torrent is seeding rather than leeching.

## Suggested fix

Pass `completedLength`/`totalLength` (or a precomputed `isComplete` flag) into `getState`/`getTorrentState`, and return `"seeding"` instead of `"leeching"` when the torrent is active but already fully downloaded:

```ts
private getTorrentState(aria2Status: Aria2Download["status"], isComplete: boolean): DownloadClientItem["state"] {
    switch (aria2Status) {
      case "active":
        return isComplete ? "seeding" : "leeching";
      ...
```

## Impact

Users monitoring their torrent client through the `downloads` widget can't tell seeding torrents apart from actively-downloading ones — everything active shows as "downloading" in the UI.
